{"name":"Jerboa","hex":"#dfb886","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jerboa","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a number of species comprising the family Dipodidae, native to the deserts of Asia and northern Africa, being a small, jumping rodent with a long tufted tail, very small forefeet and very long hind legs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jerboa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jerboa","blocks":[{"text":"Jerboas are the members of the family Dipodidae. They are nocturnal hopping desert rodents found throughout North Africa and Asia. They tend to live in hot deserts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Scarturus_euphraticus_438215030_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Scarturus_euphraticus_438215030_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerboa","wikidata":"Q273071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/LEGerbil.jpg/500px-LEGerbil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/LEGerbil.jpg/1280px-LEGerbil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/LEGerbil.jpg/500px-LEGerbil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALEGerbil.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Dipodidae_distribution.png/500px-Dipodidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Dipodidae_distribution.png/500px-Dipodidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADipodidae_distribution.pn